# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-10-kleidi/blob/ab89bcb443249e1524496b694ddb19e298dca799/src/Timelock.sol#L413-L422
https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-10-kleidi/blob/ab89bcb443249e1524496b694ddb19e298dca799/src/Timelock.sol#L589-L609
https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-10-kleidi/blob/ab89bcb443249e1524496b694ddb19e298dca799/src/Timelock.sol#L621-L665
https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-10-kleidi/blob/ab89bcb443249e1524496b694ddb19e298dca799/src/Timelock.sol#L671-L677


# Vulnerability details

## Proof of Concept
Proposals that are not executed within the expiration period are marked as expired, but the contract lacks a mechanism to handle the associated funds.
```solidity
    function isOperationExpired(bytes32 id) public view returns (bool) {
        /// if operation is done, save an extra SLOAD
        uint256 timestamp = timestamps[id];


        /// if timestamp is 0, the operation is not scheduled, revert
        require(timestamp != 0, "Timelock: operation non-existent");
        require(timestamp != 1, "Timelock: operation already executed");


        return block.timestamp >= timestamp + expirationPeriod;
    }
```
Determines if a proposal has expired based on the current block timestamp and the expiration period

Proposals can include a `value` parameter, representing native tokens (e.g., ETH) to be transferred upon execution. If a proposal expires, these funds remain in the contract without an automatic recovery mechanism.
```solidity
    function execute(
        address target,
        uint256 value,
        bytes calldata payload,
        bytes32 salt
    ) external payable whenNotPaused {
        bytes32 id = hashOperation(target, value, payload, salt);

        /// first reentrancy check, impossible to reenter and execute the same
        /// proposal twice
        require(_liveProposals.remove(id), "Timelock: proposal does not exist");
        require(isOperationReady(id), "Timelock: operation is not ready");

        _execute(target, value, payload);
        emit CallExecuted(id, 0, target, value, payload);
        /// second reentrancy check, second check that operation is ready,
        /// operation will be not ready if already executed as timestamp will
        /// be set to 1
        _afterCall(id);
    }
```
```solidity
    function executeBatch(
        address[] calldata targets,
        uint256[] calldata values,
        bytes[] calldata payloads,
        bytes32 salt
    ) external payable whenNotPaused {
        require(
            targets.length == values.length && targets.length == payloads.length,
            "Timelock: length mismatch"
        );

        bytes32 id = hashOperationBatch(targets, values, payloads, salt);

        /// first reentrancy check, impossible to reenter and execute the same
        /// proposal twice
        require(_liveProposals.remove(id), "Timelock: proposal does not exist");
        require(isOperationReady(id), "Timelock: operation is not ready");

        for (uint256 i = 0; i < targets.length; i++) {
            bytes calldata payload = payloads[i];

            _execute(targets[i], values[i], payload);
            emit CallExecuted(id, i, targets[i], values[i], payload);
        }

        /// second reentrancy check, second check that operation is ready,
        /// operation will be not ready if already executed as timestamp will
        /// be set to 1
        _afterCall(id);
    }
```
`execute` and `executeBatch` function handle the transfer of funds upon execution but do not address expired proposals.

Expired proposals are removed from the `_liveProposals` set but remain in the timestamps mapping forever.
```solidity
    function cleanup(bytes32 id) external whenNotPaused {
        require(isOperationExpired(id), "Timelock: operation not expired");
        /// unreachable state assert statement
        assert(_liveProposals.remove(id));


        emit Cleanup(id);
    }
```
The `cleanup` function removes expired proposals from `_liveProposals` but does not handle fund recovery.

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Introduce a mechanism to automatically refund the value associated with expired proposals back to the safe or original proposer.



